00:14:27.269 --> 00:14:29.290
And so this story popped into my head.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.839
It’s called Cockadoodledo

00:14:31.839 --> 00:14:35.999
Once upon a time there was a man who had a
long hard journey ahead of him.

00:14:35.999 --> 00:14:39.879
He was trudging along the way over waters
and through brushes when he saw little shiny

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:44.839
gnome with big white teeth and a black toupee
sitting by the side of the road.

00:14:44.839 --> 00:14:46.660
He was drumming on a log.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.379
With two white bones and humming oddly to
himself.

00:14:49.379 --> 00:14:55.839
The little gnome said John, why work so hard
why walk so fast.

00:14:55.839 --> 00:14:57.639
Who knows if you'll ever get there anyway.

00:14:57.639 --> 00:15:00.819
Come over here I have something to show you.

00:15:00.819 --> 00:15:02.490
So John walked off the road.

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:06.930
He was sick of walking anyway because people
kept throwing sticks and stones at him.

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:12.130
Little gnome said I have a shiny red jewel
that I would like to sell you.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:13.230
Cheap.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:15.040
Here it is.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:18.910
And from beneath his cloak he pulled the biggest
ruby that the man had ever seen.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:23.430
Must’ve weighed 100 pounds and shone like
the sun.

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.470
The gnome said, do you like it.

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:29.949
It’s an enchanted stone, what will you offer
me for it.

00:15:29.949 --> 00:15:30.949
And the man said.

00:15:30.949 --> 00:15:35.220
I don’t have much, much money but I’ll
give you everything I have.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.579
And the gnome looked displeased.

00:15:37.579 --> 00:15:41.389
So John added I could pay some more monthly.

00:15:41.389 --> 00:15:46.670
So the gnome accepted, fair enough buy now
pay later, sounds good for me, I'm all for

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:49.000
the installment plan.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.740
So the man gave the gnome all his money and
promised to pay the rest later and the gnome

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:57.779
walked back into the bush by the road clacking
his teeth and giggling and twitching.

00:15:57.779 --> 00:16:02.839
The more the man thought about this ruby and
the great deal he got the happier he became,

00:16:02.839 --> 00:16:06.459
he started back on the road with a light heart
but soon discovered that he couldn't make

00:16:06.459 --> 00:16:10.230
much progress because 100 pounds was a lot
to carry.

00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:15.199
He said to himself why continue anyways I
have what I want, I’ll just stand here holding

00:16:15.199 --> 00:16:20.529
my ruby and when people walk by they could
see how well I've all ready done.

00:16:20.529 --> 00:16:22.059
So he stopped.

00:16:22.059 --> 00:16:25.649
A little while one of his little while later
